<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24131" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-tempestīvus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>untimely</i>, <i>unseasonable</i>,
				<i>inopportune</i>, <i>inconvenient.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">postes intempestivos excisos credo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Most. 3, 2, 141</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">imbres,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					2, 873</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">929</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 1101</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amicitia numquam intempestiva est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Lael. 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">epistula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Att. 4, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cupido,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 689</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intempestivā turbantes festa
					Minervā,</span>”
				i. e. <i>by their unseasonable spinning</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib.
					4, 33</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">immodica et intempestiva libido,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vell.
					2, 68, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quid hoc joco intempestivius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 7, 8, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gula,</span>”
				<i>gratified at unseasonable times</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Vit. 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intempestivo partu extracto,</span>”
				<i>premature</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 23, 2, 17</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>that acts</i> or
				<i>does a thing unseasonably</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anseres continuo clamore intempestivi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 35, 87, § 363</span></i>
			.— <i>Adv.</i> in two forms.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> Form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intempestīvē</span></b> ,
				<i>out of season</i>, <i>unseasonably</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">accedere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Off. 1, 25</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adire ad aliquem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fam. 11, 16</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Liv. 45, 21</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fovere vulnera mentis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					P. 4, 11, 19</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 3, 19, 12</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juvare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					2, 23</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Form
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intempestīvīter</span></b> , <i>unseasonably</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dicere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					4, 20</span></i>
			
			<i>in lemm.</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
